# SWAXS Platform — example environment file
# Copy to .env for LOCAL, NON-SECRET config only. .env is git-ignored.
#
# You normally DON'T need this file: the AI Assistant reads its token, endpoint,
# and model from ~/.claude/settings.json automatically (see SECURITY.md).
#
# DO NOT put the SLAC token in this file or anywhere in the repo.
# To override the settings.json values for a session, export them in your shell:
#   export ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN="$(security find-generic-password -s slac-anthropic -w)"
#
# Non-secret overrides you *may* set here if you want:
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://ai-api.slac.stanford.edu
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6

# Optional: operator/user recorded with each reduction (else OS login is used)
# SWAXS_USER_ID=

# ── Slack notifications for unattended runs ──────────────────────────────────
# start_platform.sh sources .env automatically, and .env is git-ignored — so this
# is the right place for these. Set ONE of the two.
#
# A) Bot token — threaded updates + QC-plot uploads (recommended).
#    api.slack.com/apps → Create New App (From scratch) → OAuth & Permissions →
#    Bot Token Scopes: chat:write  (+ files:write for plots) → Install to
#    Workspace → copy the xoxb- token. Then in Slack: /invite @YourBotName
#    in the channel, and set notify.slack.channel in reactor/config.yml.
# SWAXS_SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-your-token-here
#
# B) Incoming webhook — 2 minutes, flat messages (no threading, no plots).
#    Same app → Incoming Webhooks → On → Add New Webhook to Workspace → pick the
#    channel → copy the URL. The channel is baked into the URL, so
#    notify.slack.channel is ignored in this mode.
# SWAXS_SLACK_WEBHOOK=https://hooks.slack.com/services/T000/B000/xxxx
